# Per-Dockerfile override (BuildKit convention: <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# next to the Dockerfile it applies to) for Dockerfile.lildaemon's
# `COPY lildaemon/ .` step. Build context here is Development/ (this
# file's grandparent), so paths below are relative to that root.
#
# data/, output/, and workspace/ are all bind-mounted at runtime
# (docker-compose.yml: ../lildaemon/{data,output,workspace}:/app/...), so
# baking their build-time contents into the image is pure waste — the
# mount shadows them at container start regardless. Confirmed live on
# pineal 2026-09-18: workspace/ had accumulated 1.6GB of unrelated
# leftover data (stray dagda fastText model binaries) that got copied
# into every rebuilt image and filled the host's disk.
lildaemon/data/
lildaemon/output/
lildaemon/workspace/

# Never needed in the image: dependencies come from pip install, not a
# local venv; git history has no runtime purpose.
lildaemon/.venv/
lildaemon/.git/
